@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@userId = 1
@otherUserId = 2

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Create first user
# The controller requires X-USER-ID even though createUser does not use it yet.
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "roman@example.com",
  "password": "password"
}

### Create second user
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
X-USER-ID: {{otherUserId}}

{
  "email": "second@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Get current user
# Run "Create first user" first if the database is empty.
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
X-USER-ID: {{userId}}

### Create habit for current user
POST {{baseUrl}}/habits
Content-Type: application/json
X-USER-ID: {{userId}}

{
  "name": "Drink water",
  "frequency": "daily"
}

### Create another habit for current user
POST {{baseUrl}}/habits
Content-Type: application/json
X-USER-ID: {{userId}}

{
  "name": "Read",
  "frequency": "weekly"
}

### List habits for current user
GET {{baseUrl}}/habits
X-USER-ID: {{userId}}

### List habits for second user
# Should return an empty array until you create habits with X-USER-ID: 2.
GET {{baseUrl}}/habits
X-USER-ID: {{otherUserId}}

### Missing fake auth header check
# Expected: 400 Bad Request because X-USER-ID is required.
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me

### Invalid fake auth header check
# Expected: 500 Internal Server Error unless error handling is added,
# because FakeAuthService parses X-USER-ID as a Long.
GET {{baseUrl}}/habits
X-USER-ID: not-a-number
